Reason:
The bug occurs because the runtime power management (PM) is enabled with `pm_runtime_enable(&pdev->dev);` without ensuring that it is properly disabled if an error occurs later in the probe function, specifically when the IRQ resource is missing. This leads to an unbalanced state where runtime PM remains enabled even though the device is not fully initialized, potentially causing resource management issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
ret = -EINVAL;
goto err_put_rpm;
pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
```
Reason:
The fix involves setting an error code and using a `goto` statement to jump to the error handling section, where `pm_runtime_put(&pdev->dev);` and `pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);` are called. This ensures that runtime PM is properly disabled when the probe function encounters an error, maintaining a balanced state and preventing resource management issues.

